abstract: >-
  Long-term monitoring study of a DIY 12V 500Ah LiFePO₄ battery bank
  demonstrating "architectural immunity" — the principle that parallel-connected
  mixed-brand cells achieve monolithic behavior through topology rather than
  cell matching. This dataset includes 94+ days of continuous voltage monitoring,
  ~328,000 high-frequency samples, temperature correlation analysis, and
  storage viability projections. The study validates 99.3% usable capacity
  (397 Ah) and projects 7–10 months to 80% SOC under typical parasitic loads.
